s  time yeah I was trying to represent it  the way life is I mean we don't start at  the beginning right we ever we're part  of a continuum and so it opens with but  that but that afternoon an orchestra was  playing so we are walking right into the  middle of this narrative and I and I go  back and forth and time to represent  that you know people don't just meet one  day and fall in love it's looking back  at their own histories and I think they  were there is yeah I wanted to ask you  about the young people's literature  rhetoric what is the one  you are the national ambassador for  young people's literature you've been  talking to kids all around the country  what is the message that you deliver to  them my look what I say is reading  equals hope times change and and I do  believe that when we read it gives us  hope and it changes us we're different  when we start a book and when we finish  it that is so true times change  thank you very much I was like this is  why we today
 

